        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Regulation is choosing how to respond to an emotion instead of being driven by it. It does not mean suppressing feelings; it means creating a pause between the trigger and your response.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Pause, breathe slowly and name the emotion before you respond.\n\u2022 Reframe the situation: ask what else could explain what happened.\n\u2022 Suppressed emotions tend to leak out later; acknowledge them, then choose your action.\n\nTry this\nPick one recurring trigger at work. Plan a specific pause routine (for example three slow breaths and one question) and use it the next time.",
