        "body":
            "The breath is a simple anchor for attention because it is always available. Training attention on the breath strengthens your ability to notice distraction and return to the task.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Slow breathing with a longer out-breath calms the nervous system.\n\u2022 When attention wanders, gently bring it back without criticism.\n\u2022 Single-tasking produces better work than constant switching.\n\nTry this\nBefore your next focused task, take five breaths counting four in and six out, then work for 25 minutes without switching.",
