        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lmyZMtPVodo",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Leading Teams\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-9",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reading: Leading Teams",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Teams perform best when people feel safe to speak up, know what is expected and believe their leader has their back.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Set clear goals, roles and standards.\n\u2022 Recognise effort and progress specifically and often.\n\u2022 Invite dissent and thank people who raise concerns.\n\nTry this\nHold a short one-to-one with each team member and ask: \"What is one thing I could do to help you do your best work?\"",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-10",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reflection worksheet",
        "type": "document",
        "url": "assets/materials/leadership/worksheet.docx",
        "fileName": "worksheet.docx",
        "body":
            "Download the Word worksheet, answer the reflection questions and keep it for your records.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-11",
        "module": 3,
        "title":
            "Watch: The surprising habits of original thinkers (Adam Grant, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fxbCHn6gE3U",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Decision-Making\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-12",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Reading: Decision-Making",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Good decisions balance speed and quality. Leaders gather diverse views, separate facts from assumptions and are clear about who decides and how.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Decide how a decision will be made before debating options.\n\u2022 Seek out views that disagree with your first instinct.\n\u2022 Review important decisions afterwards to learn from them.\n\nTry this\nFor your next significant decision, list the facts, the assumptions and two alternative options before choosing.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-13",
        "module": 3,
        "title":
            "Further reading: Leading change: why transformation efforts fail (John Kotter, HBR)",
        "type": "link",
        "url":
            "https://hbr.org/2007/01/leading-change-why-transformation-efforts-fail",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Read this article to go deeper into the ideas from this module.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-14",
        "module": 4,
        "title":
            "Watch: Forget the pecking order at work (Margaret Heffernan, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vyn_xLrtZaY",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Creating High-Performing Teams\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-15",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Reading: Creating High-Performing Teams",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "High-performing teams rely on helpfulness and social connection more than on star individuals. Leaders build this through shared goals, trust and continuous learning.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Helpfulness between team members drives results.\n\u2022 Shared goals beat individual competition.\n\u2022 Regular retrospectives turn experience into improvement.\n\nTry this\nRun a 20-minute team retrospective: what went well, what did not, and one change to try next.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "leadership-16",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Action plan",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/leadership/action-plan.pdf",
        "fileName": "action-plan.pdf",
        "body":
            "Turn what you learned into specific actions with dates. Print it or fill it in on screen.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
    ],
