  "communication": {
    "lessons": [
      {
        "id": "communication-1",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Welcome to the course",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "assets/materials/communication/welcome.mp4",
        "fileName": "welcome.mp4",
        "body":
            "A short welcome to Effective Communication: how the course works and how to earn your certificate.",
        "minutes": 1,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-2",
        "module": 0,
        "title":
            "Watch: 10 ways to have a better conversation (Celeste Headlee, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R1vskiVDwl4",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Foundations of Communication\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-3",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Reading: Foundations of Communication",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Communication is successful when the message received matches the message intended. That depends on clarity, attention and the relationship between the people involved.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Know your purpose and audience before you speak or write.\n\u2022 Be present: avoid multitasking in conversations.\n\u2022 Check understanding instead of assuming it.\n\nTry this\nBefore three important messages this week, write the one thing you want the other person to know or do.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-4",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Course slides",
        "type": "slides",
        "url": "assets/materials/communication/slides.pptx",
        "fileName": "slides.pptx",
        "body":
            "Slide deck covering every module. Open it full screen or download it for later.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-5",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Watch: 5 ways to listen better (Julian Treasure, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cSohjlYQI2A",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Active Listening\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-6",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Reading: Active Listening",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Active listening means giving full attention, showing you are listening and confirming what you understood. It builds trust and prevents costly misunderstandings.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Use open questions: what, how, tell me more.\n\u2022 Paraphrase: \"So what you are saying is ...\"\n\u2022 Notice emotion as well as content.\n\nTry this\nIn one conversation a day, paraphrase the other person before you share your own view.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-7",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Learner workbook",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/communication/workbook.pdf",
        "fileName": "workbook.pdf",
        "body":
            "Summaries, key ideas, practice activities and space for your notes for each module.",
        "minutes": 20,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-8",
        "module": 2,
        "title":
            "Watch: How to speak so that people want to listen (Julian Treasure, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eIho2S0ZahI",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Clear and Confident Speaking\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-9",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reading: Clear and Confident Speaking",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Clear speakers lead with the main point, use simple language and support it with one or two concrete examples. Voice, pace and pauses add confidence.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Lead with the conclusion, then give the reasons.\n\u2022 Replace jargon with plain words.\n\u2022 Slow down and pause after key points.\n\nTry this\nRecord a two-minute update, listen back and cut one filler habit.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-10",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reflection worksheet",
        "type": "document",
        "url": "assets/materials/communication/worksheet.docx",
        "fileName": "worksheet.docx",
        "body":
            "Download the Word worksheet, answer the reflection questions and keep it for your records.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-11",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Watch: The walk from \"no\" to \"yes\" (William Ury, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hc6yi_FtoNo",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Difficult Conversations\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-12",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Reading: Difficult Conversations",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Difficult conversations go better when you prepare, focus on interests rather than positions and stay curious about the other person's view.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Separate the person from the problem.\n\u2022 Describe behaviour and impact, not character.\n\u2022 Look for a shared interest you can both agree on.\n\nTry this\nPlan one conversation you have been avoiding: the facts, the impact and the outcome you want.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-13",
        "module": 3,
        "title":
            "Further reading: Active listening (Center for Creative Leadership)",
        "type": "link",
        "url":
            "https://www.ccl.org/articles/leading-effectively-articles/coaching-others-use-active-listening-skills/",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Read this article to go deeper into the ideas from this module.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-14",
        "module": 4,
        "title":
            "Watch: Your body language may shape who you are (Amy Cuddy, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ks-_Mh1QhMc",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Professional Communication\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-15",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Reading: Professional Communication",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Professional communication is clear, respectful and suited to the channel. Body language, email tone and meeting habits all shape how your message lands.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Choose the channel: urgent or sensitive topics deserve a conversation.\n\u2022 Write emails with a clear subject, purpose and next step.\n\u2022 Open posture and eye contact signal confidence and respect.\n\nTry this\nRewrite one long email so the request and deadline appear in the first two lines.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "communication-16",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Action plan",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/communication/action-plan.pdf",
        "fileName": "action-plan.pdf",
        "body":
            "Turn what you learned into specific actions with dates. Print it or fill it in on screen.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
    ],
