  "workplace-wellbeing": {
    "lessons": [
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-1",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Welcome to the course",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "assets/materials/workplace-wellbeing/welcome.mp4",
        "fileName": "welcome.mp4",
        "body":
            "A short welcome to Workplace Well-being: how the course works and how to earn your certificate.",
        "minutes": 1,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-2",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Watch: The happy secret to better work (Shawn Achor, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fLJsdqxnZb0",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Understanding Workplace Well-being\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-3",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Reading: Understanding Workplace Well-being",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Well-being at work covers physical, mental and social health. It affects engagement, performance and retention, and it is shaped by both individual habits and the way work is designed.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Well-being is physical, mental, social and financial.\n\u2022 A positive mindset improves productivity and creativity.\n\u2022 Organisations and individuals share responsibility.\n\nTry this\nRate your energy, sleep, connection and workload from 1 to 10 and note the lowest one.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-4",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Course slides",
        "type": "slides",
        "url": "assets/materials/workplace-wellbeing/slides.pptx",
        "fileName": "slides.pptx",
        "body":
            "Slide deck covering every module. Open it full screen or download it for later.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-5",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Watch: How to make stress your friend (Kelly McGonigal, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RcGyVTAoXEU",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Managing Stress\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-6",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Reading: Managing Stress",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Short-term stress can sharpen performance, but chronic stress harms health. Managing stress means recognising your signals, reducing avoidable pressure and building recovery into the day.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Know your personal early warning signs.\n\u2022 Separate what you can control from what you cannot.\n\u2022 Reach out: connection buffers the effects of stress.\n\nTry this\nList your current pressures in two columns: within my control and outside my control. Act on one item in the first column.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-7",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Learner workbook",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/workplace-wellbeing/workbook.pdf",
        "fileName": "workbook.pdf",
        "body":
            "Summaries, key ideas, practice activities and space for your notes for each module.",
        "minutes": 20,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-8",
        "module": 2,
        "title":
            "Watch: Inside the mind of a master procrastinator (Tim Urban, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=arj7oStGLkU",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Healthy Work Practices\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-9",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reading: Healthy Work Practices",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Healthy work practices include realistic planning, regular breaks, movement and clear boundaries between work and rest. Small changes repeated daily make the biggest difference.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Plan your top three priorities each day.\n\u2022 Take a short break every 60 to 90 minutes.\n\u2022 Set boundaries for messages outside working hours.\n\nTry this\nBlock two 90-minute focus periods in your calendar this week and protect them.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-10",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reflection worksheet",
        "type": "document",
        "url": "assets/materials/workplace-wellbeing/worksheet.docx",
        "fileName": "worksheet.docx",
        "body":
            "Download the Word worksheet, answer the reflection questions and keep it for your records.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-11",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Watch: How to practice emotional first aid (Guy Winch, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F2hc2FLOdhI",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Resilience at Work\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-12",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Reading: Resilience at Work",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Resilience is the ability to adapt and recover from setbacks. It is built through supportive relationships, self-compassion, perspective and taking care of the basics.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Treat yourself as you would treat a friend after a setback.\n\u2022 Interrupt rumination by doing something absorbing.\n\u2022 Keep sleep, movement and nutrition steady under pressure.\n\nTry this\nRecall a past setback you recovered from and write down three things that helped.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-13",
        "module": 3,
        "title":
            "Further reading: Coping with stress at work (American Psychological Association)",
        "type": "link",
        "url": "https://www.apa.org/topics/healthy-workplaces/work-stress",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Read this article to go deeper into the ideas from this module.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-14",
        "module": 4,
        "title":
            "Watch: What makes us feel good about our work? (Dan Ariely, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5aH2Ppjpcho",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Creating a Well-being Culture\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-15",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Reading: Creating a Well-being Culture",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "A well-being culture makes healthy choices the norm: fair workloads, recognition, meaningful work and leaders who model balance.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Acknowledgement and meaning increase motivation.\n\u2022 Leaders model behaviour: their habits set the norms.\n\u2022 Check in on workload regularly, not only in crises.\n\nTry this\nRecognise one colleague specifically this week for effort, not only results.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "workplace-wellbeing-16",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Action plan",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/workplace-wellbeing/action-plan.pdf",
        "fileName": "action-plan.pdf",
        "body":
            "Turn what you learned into specific actions with dates. Print it or fill it in on screen.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
    ],
