      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-3",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Reading: Self-Awareness",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Personal growth starts with an honest view of your strengths, values and patterns. Being open about what you do not know makes learning and connection possible.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Identify your top strengths and how you use them.\n\u2022 Clarify your values: what matters most to you?\n\u2022 Vulnerability is a source of courage and connection.\n\nTry this\nAsk three people: \"What do you think I do best?\" Look for the common theme.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-4",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Course slides",
        "type": "slides",
        "url": "assets/materials/personal-development/slides.pptx",
        "fileName": "slides.pptx",
        "body":
            "Slide deck covering every module. Open it full screen or download it for later.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-5",
        "module": 1,
        "title":
            "Watch: Grit: the power of passion and perseverance (Angela Lee Duckworth, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H14bBuluwB8",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Personal Goals\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-6",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Reading: Personal Goals",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Good goals are specific, meaningful and broken into steps. Perseverance towards long-term goals matters as much as talent.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Use SMART goals: specific, measurable, achievable, relevant, time-bound.\n\u2022 Link each goal to a value so it stays meaningful.\n\u2022 Break big goals into weekly actions.\n\nTry this\nWrite one SMART goal for the next 90 days and the first action you will take this week.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-7",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Learner workbook",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/personal-development/workbook.pdf",
        "fileName": "workbook.pdf",
        "body":
            "Summaries, key ideas, practice activities and space for your notes for each module.",
        "minutes": 20,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-8",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Watch: Try something new for 30 days (Matt Cutts, TED-Ed)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UNP03fDSj1U",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Building Positive Habits\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-9",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reading: Building Positive Habits",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Habits turn intentions into results. Start small, attach the new habit to an existing cue and track your streak.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Make the habit small enough to do on a bad day.\n\u2022 Use a cue: \"After I ..., I will ...\"\n\u2022 Track progress to stay motivated.\n\nTry this\nChoose one 30-day challenge and mark each day you complete it.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-10",
        "module": 2,
        "title": "Reflection worksheet",
        "type": "document",
        "url": "assets/materials/personal-development/worksheet.docx",
        "fileName": "worksheet.docx",
        "body":
            "Download the Word worksheet, answer the reflection questions and keep it for your records.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-11",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Watch: The power of introverts (Susan Cain, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c0KYU2j0TM4",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Confidence and Growth\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-12",
        "module": 3,
        "title": "Reading: Confidence and Growth",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Confidence grows from evidence of your own progress and from working with your natural style rather than against it.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Collect evidence of progress in a \"wins\" log.\n\u2022 Play to your natural style: quiet strengths are strengths.\n\u2022 Step slightly outside your comfort zone regularly.\n\nTry this\nKeep a wins log for two weeks: one thing each day you did well or learned.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-13",
        "module": 3,
        "title":
            "Further reading: Building your resilience (American Psychological Association)",
        "type": "link",
        "url": "https://www.apa.org/topics/resilience/building-your-resilience",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Read this article to go deeper into the ideas from this module.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-14",
        "module": 4,
        "title":
            "Watch: The power of believing that you can improve (Carol Dweck, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_X0mgOOSpLU",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Continuous Improvement\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-15",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Reading: Continuous Improvement",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Continuous improvement means regularly reviewing what works, seeking feedback and adjusting. A growth mindset keeps you learning after setbacks.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Review monthly: keep, stop, start.\n\u2022 Ask for feedback on one specific behaviour.\n\u2022 Treat mistakes as data for the next attempt.\n\nTry this\nDo a keep, stop, start review of your last month and pick one change.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "personal-development-16",
        "module": 4,
        "title": "Action plan",
        "type": "pdf",
        "url": "assets/materials/personal-development/action-plan.pdf",
        "fileName": "action-plan.pdf",
        "body":
            "Turn what you learned into specific actions with dates. Print it or fill it in on screen.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
    ],
