  "organisational-development": {
    "lessons": [
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-1",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Welcome to the course",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "assets/materials/organisational-development/welcome.mp4",
        "fileName": "welcome.mp4",
        "body":
            "A short welcome to Organisational Development: how the course works and how to earn your certificate.",
        "minutes": 1,
      },
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-2",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Watch: The puzzle of motivation (Dan Pink, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rrkrvAUbU9Y",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Introduction to Organisational Development\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-3",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Reading: Introduction to Organisational Development",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Organisational development (OD) is a planned, evidence-based effort to improve how an organisation works. It focuses on people, culture, structure and processes together.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 OD is planned, organisation-wide and based on data.\n\u2022 Intrinsic motivation (autonomy, mastery, purpose) drives modern work.\n\u2022 Diagnose before you intervene.\n\nTry this\nList one organisational problem and three sources of data you could use to understand it better.",
        "minutes": 10,
      },
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-4",
        "module": 0,
        "title": "Course slides",
        "type": "slides",
        "url": "assets/materials/organisational-development/slides.pptx",
        "fileName": "slides.pptx",
        "body":
            "Slide deck covering every module. Open it full screen or download it for later.",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-5",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Watch: Are you a giver or a taker? (Adam Grant, TED)",
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YyXRYgjQXX0",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Watch this talk and note one idea you can use in your work. It supports the module \"Organisational Culture\".",
        "minutes": 15,
      },
      {
        "id": "organisational-development-6",
        "module": 1,
        "title": "Reading: Organisational Culture",
        "type": "reading",
        "url": "",
        "fileName": "",
        "body":
            "Culture is \"how we do things around here\": shared values, beliefs and behaviours. It shows in what gets rewarded, tolerated and talked about.\n\nKey ideas\n\u2022 Culture is visible in behaviour, rituals and decisions.\n\u2022 Generous, helpful cultures outperform over time.\n\u2022 Leaders shape culture most through what they reward.\n\nTry this\nWrite down three behaviours that are rewarded in your organisation and one that should be.",
        "minutes": 10,
